{
  "$comment": "Per-million-token rates in USD. Verified against https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/docs/about-claude/pricing (see specs/003-accurate-workflow-summary/pricing-verified.md). 5-minute cache TTL assumed. Entries ordered longest-prefix-first; patterns use * (no required separator) so they match both the bare id (claude-opus-4-6), dated suffix (claude-opus-4-6-20250929), and context-window suffix (claude-opus-4-6[1m]) so minor-version-specific families win over the broad family wildcard.",
  "$ordering_contract": "ARRAY ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING AND IS TESTED. workflow_summary_lib.match_family() returns the FIRST array-order regex match, and a family pattern is a prefix glob, so `claude-opus-5*` matches `claude-opus-5-5-20260901` just as happily as `claude-opus-5`. Whenever one family's pattern is a prefix of another's, the MORE SPECIFIC one must appear first or the broader one silently swallows it and prices it wrong — e.g. Opus 5.5 ($4/$20) billed as Opus 5 ($5/$25), with no error and no log line. tests/activity/test_usage.py asserts this for every prefix pair in the file; do not reorder without running it. Rates are NEVER derived: cache read is 0.1x base input for most families but 0.025x for Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1 and 0.05x for Opus 5.5, so a derived table would overprice Fable 5.1 cache reads 4x.",
  "fallback_order": [
    "exact",
    "minor",
    "major",
    "tier"
  ],
